==Icelandic==

===Pronoun===
{{infl|is|indefinite pronoun|g=m}} (''feminine'' '''[[#Icelandic|einhver]]''', ''neuter'' '''[[eitthvert]]''' ''or'' '''[[eitthvað]]''')

# {{context|indefinite}} [[somebody]], [[some]], [[someone]], [[something]] (abbreviation '''[[e-h]]''')
#: ''Þekkir þú '''einhvern''' sem notar Linux?''
#:: Do you know '''someone''' who uses Linux?
#: ''Ég kann '''eitthvað''' í japönsku.''
#:: I know '''a little''' Japanese.
# feminine {{nominative}} {{singular}} of '''einhver'''
# neuter {{nominative}} {{plural}} of '''einhver'''
# neuter {{accusative}} {{plural}} of '''einhver'''

====Declension====
{{Icelandic indefinite pronoun}}

====Derived terms====
* [[að einhverju leyti]] (in part)
* [[einhvern daginn]]
* [[einhvern tíma]]
* [[einhverju sinni]]
* [[einhvern veginn]]

====Usage notes====
* The neuter singular form {{term|eitthvert|lang=is}} is used [[demonstrative]]ly ({{term|hliðstæður|hliðstætt|lang=is}}), i.e. with a [[noun]] while the neuter singular form {{term|eitthvað|lang=is}} is used [[substantive]]ly ({{term|sérstæður|sérstætt|lang=is}}):
*: ''Heyrðirðu '''eitthvað'''?''
*:: Did you hear '''something'''?
*: ''[http://visindavefur.hi.is/svar.asp?id=3178 Er '''eitthvert''' sannleikskorn í grísku goðsögunum]?''
*:: Is there '''some''' grain of truth to the Greek myths?

